course: dictionary
lesson: 7418
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives polecat three meanings, and the sentence around the word tells you which one is meant. «Sousliks are a main food for steppe eagles, imperial eagles and steppe polecats» is about animals that eat sousliks, so here a polecat is an animal.
explain: Look for clues in the rest of the text. «Little sousliks do the same, and eagles and polecats hunt them.» Hunting is something animals do, so the clue points to the animal meaning again. Always ask: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Meanings can also change from place to place. In the USA, polecat can mean a skunk, which is a different animal. Long ago, calling someone a polecat meant they were nasty. If you are not sure, read on and look for the clues.
fact: A polecat is a wild animal of the weasel family, with dark brown fur and a pale face mask.
fact: A polecat gives off a strong smell when it is frightened.
fact: Polecats are carnivores, which means they eat other animals.
fact: The pet ferret comes from the European polecat.
fact: In the USA, «polecat» is an old country word for a skunk.
exercise: «Sousliks are a main food for steppe eagles, imperial eagles and steppe polecats.» In this sentence, what is a polecat? | A small bird with a pale face | *A wild animal that hunts other animals | A nasty person | A kind of skunk in the USA
exercise: In «eagles and polecats hunt them», what does the word hunt tell you about polecats? | They sleep all day in holes | They are people who are rude | They live in a town | *They are animals that chase and eat other animals
exercise: Why does the meaning of polecat change from place to place? | *Because one word can have different meanings in different places | Because the dictionary has a mistake | Because polecats move to a new country every year | Because polecats are always called skunks
test: Which meaning of polecat is about the animal's smell? | *It gives off a strong smell when frightened | It is a long word with no meaning | It is a fish that swims in rivers | It is a bird that flies over the steppe
test: Why must you check the words around a word like polecat? | *Because one word can have more than one meaning | Because polecat is only found in a dictionary | Because you should never guess | Because the words around it are always wrong
exam: «Sousliks are a main food for steppe eagles, imperial eagles and steppe polecats.» In this sentence, what kind of word is polecat? | A name for a town | *A noun meaning an animal | A verb meaning to run away | An adjective meaning brown
